. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H4 * 
.         
.         * Variable of interest: To determine whether or not having at least o
> ne daugher has a
.         * different effect on male/female respondents we need to include the 
> interaction term
.         * between gender and the variable of interest. 
.         
.         gen     inter = female * d_daughter

.         
.         * Then, we use OLS to regress attitudes towards gender equality on "h
> aving at least one daughter"
.         * Our specification includes controls for the respondent's gender (fe
> male), age, age2/100, 
.         * level of education, marital status, employment status, income, reli
> gion, East Germany, 
.         * and emigrant. The dependent variable in the analysis is plh0395avg 
> as defined above.
.         
.         reg plh0395avg d_daughter female inter age age2 i.pgisced11 i.pgfamst
> d i.pgemplst i.plh0258_h i.hgnuts1_ew  Germany log_pglabnet, robust

